{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":43,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.familyWellDefined_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.familyWellDefined_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L457-L470","doc":"**The definitions are not vacuous, in both directions.** A constant family is\nwell-defined; the identity family on `ℤ` with two distinct resolutions is\nnot. Without this pair, everything above would be consistent with the\npredicates being unsatisfiable or trivially satisfiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.wellDefined_of_const_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.wellDefined_of_const_zero","kind":"theorem","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L447-L455","doc":"**A member that vanishes everywhere is constant VACUOUSLY.**\n\n`μ̄₁₂₃ = 0` on both recorded branches, so it *is* well-defined on its own —\nand this says so, to make precise that the agreement is the zero, not a\nstructural property. Composed with the theorem above, it is the whole point:\na vanishing member is well-defined while the family is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.not_familyWellDefined_of_one_member_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.not_familyWellDefined_of_one_member_ne","kind":"theorem","line":437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L437-L445","doc":"**ONE branch-dependent member refutes the whole family.**\n\nThis is the load-bearing statement. `lk` is measured branch-dependent, so the\nMilnor family is not well-defined on the atom element — and that is settled\n*before* any higher rung is computed. Walking the ladder cannot repair it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.not_wellDefinedOnResolutions_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.not_wellDefinedOnResolutions_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L430-L435","doc":"**Two resolutions with different values refute well-definedness.** This is\nthe shape of the `lk` measurement: exhibit the σ and σ⁻¹ branches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.FamilyWellDefinedOnResolutions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.FamilyWellDefinedOnResolutions","kind":"def","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L423-L428","doc":"A **family** of invariants is well-defined on the element when every member\nis. This is the right object: a route does not consume one invariant, it\nconsumes a ladder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.WellDefinedOnResolutions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.WellDefinedOnResolutions","kind":"def","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L417-L421","doc":"An invariant is **well-defined on a superposed element** exactly when it is\nconstant across the element's resolutions. `R` indexes resolutions, `res`\nsends each to the link it resolves to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.no_asymmetry_of_all_triples_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.no_asymmetry_of_all_triples_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L329-L333","doc":"**Hence no charge-antisymmetric content**: the mirror difference this route\nwould have to supply is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.constant_of_all_triples_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.constant_of_all_triples_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L317-L327","doc":"**The same, for a functional of the WHOLE family of triples** — which is the\nescape a reader reaches for when told one triple vanishes.\n\n`κ` indexes the triples; `μ i` is the isotope's full vector of triple\ninvariants. The probe's result is `∀ i t, μ i t = 0`, so the vectors are\nequal and any `F` whatever — symmetric function, norm, maximum — is constant\nacross isotopes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.constant_of_vanishing_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.constant_of_vanishing_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L306-L315","doc":"**A functional of an invariant that vanishes across a family is constant on\nit** — so it supplies neither a difference between two members nor an\nA-dependent profile.\n\nInstantiate `ι` at the isotopes and `μ` at `μ̄₁₂₃` of a chosen triple: with\nthe probe's measured `hμ`, every `E_EM` built from `μ̄₁₂₃` — **including every\neven one** — takes the same value at ³H and ³He. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.exchange_symmetry_forces_agreement_on_pm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.exchange_symmetry_forces_agreement_on_pm_one","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L246-L265","doc":"**The sharper reading, and the one that constrains route (2).**  Exchange\nsymmetry *alone* — with no parity assumption at all — forces any admissible\nfunctional to take the **same value** on the Borromean longitude and on its\ncomponent-swapped partner.\n\nSince those two are separated by `μ̄₁₂₃ = 1` against `μ̄₁₂₃ = -1`\n(`mubar_separates_borromean_from_unlink` gives the analogous separation from\nthe unlink), the consequence is that **the sign of `μ̄₁₂₃` is invisible to any\nexchange-symmetric `E_EM`**: on this pair such a functional sees at most\n`|μ̄₁₂₃|`.\n\nThat is strictly stronger than \"odd functionals vanish\", which is the special\ncase `F (-m) = - F m`.  For route (2) it says the triple-linking channel can\nsupply a *magnitude* to the EM weight but never a *chirality*, so any\nconstruction whose EM content is carried by the sign of `μ̄₁₂₃` is excluded\nbefore it is built. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.even_symmetric_functional_can_be_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.even_symmetric_functional_can_be_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L233-L244","doc":"**The prune is not vacuous in the even direction**: an even, exchange-\nsymmetric functional can be nonzero at the Borromean configuration.  Witness\n`F m = m ^ 2`.\n\nWithout this the pair of theorems above would be consistent with *every*\nadmissible functional vanishing, which would kill route (2) rather than\nnarrow it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.even_functional_is_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.even_functional_is_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L223-L231","doc":"An **even** functional satisfies the exchange-symmetry hypothesis\nautomatically — it does not have to be imposed.\n\nSo evenness is not a constraint the route must additionally satisfy; it is the\ncondition under which the exchange symmetry is free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.linear_coefficient_must_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.linear_coefficient_must_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L207-L213","doc":"The linear case spelled out, since it is the ansatz anyone writes first:\nan exchange-symmetric `E_EM = c · μ̄₁₂₃` forces `c = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.odd_symmetric_functional_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.odd_symmetric_functional_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L189-L205","doc":"**The second prune for 4-B.** Any functional of `μ̄₁₂₃` that is *odd* and\n*symmetric under exchanging the two like-charged components* vanishes.\n\nA two-like-charge Coulomb self-energy is symmetric under that exchange, so this\nforbids every `E_EM` odd in `μ̄₁₂₃` — in particular every `E_EM` **linear** in\nit, which is the obvious first ansatz. The map must be even.\n\nThe physics input consumed here is only that the self-energy is exchange-\nsymmetric; the antisymmetry of `μ̄₁₂₃` is computed above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_swap_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_swap_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L185-L187","doc":"**Exchange antisymmetry**, computed rather than quoted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_swapped_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_swapped_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L182-L183","doc":"`μ̄₁₂₃ = −1` after exchanging the two like-charged components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.swappedLongitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.swappedLongitude","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L179-L180","doc":"The longitude with components `1` and `2` exchanged: `[x₂, x₁]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.noncommutator_degree_one_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.noncommutator_degree_one_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L157-L166","doc":"**Control on the hypothesis.** The non-commutator word `x₁x₂` also has\n`X₁X₂`-coefficient `1`, but its degree-1 part is nonzero — so it does *not*\nsatisfy the vanishing-linking condition, and reading a `μ̄₁₂₃` off it would be\nreading an indeterminate quantity.\n\nThis is here so the `= 1` above is not mistaken for \"any word gives 1\": the\nvalue is meaningful for the commutator *because* its degree-1 part vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_separates_borromean_from_unlink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_separates_borromean_from_unlink","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L151-L155","doc":"**The separation the prune asked for.** Pairwise linking assigns the\nBorromean braid and the unlink the same data;\n`μ̄₁₂₃` does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_unlink_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_unlink_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L147-L149","doc":"`μ̄₁₂₃ = 0` on the unlink, so the invariant separates the two links that\npairwise linking could not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_borromean_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_borromean_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L142-L145","doc":"**`μ̄₁₂₃ = 1` on the Borromean braid** — the invariant the pairwise prune\nleaves standing. (Not a new value: `binding_mn_milnor_linking.py` already\ncomputes it. This is the Lean port.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.magnus_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.magnus_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L133-L140","doc":"The full degree-2 expansion of the commutator is `1 + X₁X₂ − X₂X₁`.\n\nNote `c1 = c2 = 0`: the degree-1 part vanishes. Those coefficients are the\nlinking numbers, so this reproduces `BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borromean_crossSum_zero`\nby an entirely different route — and it is exactly the hypothesis under which\n`μ̄₁₂₃` is indeterminacy-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.unlinkLongitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.unlinkLongitude","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L130-L131","doc":"The unlink: trivial longitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.borromeanLongitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.borromeanLongitude","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L127-L128","doc":"The Borromean longitude `[x₁, x₂] = x₁x₂x₁⁻¹x₂⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar123","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar123","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L124-L125","doc":"Milnor's `μ̄₁₂₃`: the coefficient of `X₁X₂` in the longitude's expansion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.magnus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.magnus","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L119-L122","doc":"Magnus expansion of a word, truncated at degree 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.genImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.genImage","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L111-L117","doc":"Magnus image of a single letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Gen","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L108-L109","doc":"A free-group letter: generator index (`1` or `2`) and whether it is inverted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.mul","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L95-L104","doc":"Truncated product. `X₁X₂ ≠ X₂X₁`, so `c12` and `c21` are tracked separately —\nwhich is the whole point: `μ̄₁₂₃` lives in the difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.one","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instReprDeg2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instReprDeg2","kind":"instance","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instReprDeg2.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instReprDeg2.repr","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instDecidableEqDeg2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instDecidableEqDeg2","kind":"instance","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instDecidableEqDeg2.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.instDecidableEqDeg2.decEq","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.c22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.c22","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.c21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.Deg2.c21","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnot